=== meta
profile = "geml-style/v1"
title = "codemap style entry"
default-style = "style.geml"
===

This map's **style entry point** — one fixed path, `_index/index.geml`, for any
GEML root. `default-style` names the stylesheet every document in this root uses.

There is no `#sitemap` table here, and that is the point: every document gets the
same stylesheet, so listing them one by one would be 37 rows saying the same
thing. Add the table only when some document needs a DIFFERENT stylesheet:

  === table {#sitemap}
  | document | template |
  |---|---|
  | index.geml | overview.geml |
  ===

Resolution is two steps and no more: an exact `#sitemap` row wins, otherwise
`default-style`. No glob, no cascade, no source order — the same arbitration
rule the `geml-style/v1` profile applies to selectors, applied to documents.
